/-!
# Existence of content ideals over a valuation ring

Let `A → B` be a local ring map of local rings which is essentially of finite type and let `N` be
a finite `B`-module which is flat as an `A`-module. If `A` is a valuation ring then every element
of `N` has a content ideal `I ⊆ A` in the sense of Stacks 0ASA, and `I` is principal. This file
proves both assertions. The valuation ring `A` need not be henselian, so Stacks 05U7 does not
apply to `N` over `A` directly, and the whole argument is the descent of the content ideal along
the henselization `A ⊆ Aʰ`.

## Main results

* `exists_isContentIdeal_of_valuationRing`: every element of `N` has a content ideal.
* `exists_isContentIdeal_isPrincipal_of_valuationRing_of_flat`: Stacks 0ASX, both assertions
  together: every element of `N` has a content ideal, and it is principal.

## Implementation notes

The source proves existence by passing to the henselization `Aʰ` of `A` and to the localization
`B'` of `B ⊗_A Aʰ` at `𝔪_B ⊗ Aʰ + B ⊗ 𝔪_{Aʰ}`, where Stacks 05U7 does apply: `Aʰ` is henselian,
`B'` is essentially of finite type and local over it, and `N' = N ⊗_B B'` is a finite `B'`-module
flat over `Aʰ`. An element of `N` lies in `I N` exactly when its image lies in `I N'`, because
`B → B'` is faithfully flat, and `I ↦ I Aʰ` is an inclusion-preserving bijection on ideals; so a
content ideal upstairs descends to one downstairs. The descent is done here in full.

Upstairs the content ideal comes from `Module.exists_isContentIdeal_of_colimit_free_presentation`
(`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Flat.ContentIdealFromColimitFree`), which is Stacks 05U7 over the
henselian base followed by Stacks 0ASD. Its universe parameters are the ones the descent
consumes: the henselization of `A` and the localization of `B ⊗_A Aʰ` both live in
`Type (max u v)`, and the module `B' ⊗_B N` in `Type (max u v w)`, which is the universe in which
the three auxiliary universes of the Mittag-Leffler condition of Stacks 059F are taken.

Principality is `IsContentIdeal.isPrincipal_of_valuationRing`: a content ideal is finitely
generated by Stacks 0ASB, and a valuation ring is Bézout by Stacks 090Q.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ASX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ASX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ASA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ASA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ASB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ASB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0ASD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0ASD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05U7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05U7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 090Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/090Q)
-/

@[expose] public section

